                <pb facs="0332" n="247" sameAs="frus:frus1919v02/pg247"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">033.4111/68: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Davis</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of
                            State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-07-03T13:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">July 3, 1919, 1
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">Received 1.55
                            p.m.</hi>]</dateline></opener>
                <p>2456. Having learned the Prince of Wales expected a formal and official call from
                    me with reference to the invitation to America, I <pb facs="0333" n="248"
                        xml:id="pg248"/> have called on him this morning and presented verbally and
                    in writing a formal invitation in the name of the President. Up to last night
                    the communication from the British Embassy had not been received by the Foreign
                    Office. The Prince accepts gladly but thinks that according to the present plans
                    he will not be able to come until October and probably only to Washington.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Davis</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
